---
description: Accessibility rules — WCAG AA minimum, non-negotiable for a medical site
alwaysApply: true
---

- Every interactive element (buttons, links, form fields, accordion triggers, carousel
  controls, the WhatsApp button) must be reachable and operable via keyboard alone, in
  a logical tab order, and must show a visible focus ring (never `outline: none` without
  a replacement focus style).
- All images require descriptive, specific alt text tied to the medical context (e.g.
  "Dental implant procedure room with overhead light," not "dentist" or "" ).
  Purely decorative background shapes/blobs get `alt=""` or `aria-hidden="true"`.
- All form fields must have an associated, visible `<label>` — placeholder text alone is
  never an acceptable substitute for a label.
- All icon-only buttons/links (social icons, close buttons, carousel arrows) must have a
  descriptive `aria-label`.
- Maintain WCAG AA color contrast: 4.5:1 for normal text, 3:1 for large text (18px+ or
  14px+ bold), checked against the actual theme background, not assumed.
- Use correct landmark elements and heading hierarchy: one `<h1>` per page, `<nav>` for
  navigation, `<footer>` for the footer, `<main>` wrapping page content — don't skip
  heading levels (no jumping from `<h2>` to `<h4>`).
- Modals/dialogs (lightbox, mobile nav drawer) must trap focus while open and return
  focus to the triggering element on close, and must be dismissible via `Escape`.
- Any content-hiding entrance animation must not prevent screen readers or keyboard
  users from reaching the content immediately — don't rely on animation-driven visibility
  toggles that also block assistive tech.
